  "query_preview": "../Monday through Thursday/...Continuing to see a \nstrong low in the southern gulf, generating long term near gale to\nstrong gale force southeast winds offshore of Prince of Wales \nIsland. At this time, Monday looks the strongest, with gales \naround 40-45 knots in the southern zones and up to 30 knot \nnortherlies in the inner channels. As for precipitation, expect to\nsee multiple waves of precipitation moves up from the south over \nthe panhandle. These waves of moisture will be pushing through \nconstant ridging and easterly winds aloft causing warming and \ndrying. As such, overall PoP chances are very uncertain, with much\nof the southern panhandle to Icy Strait keeping between 30-70%. \nOne interesting portion of this forecast though is the possibility\nfor mixing on the leading edge of the mostly rain. If it does \noccur, and it is fairly unlikely at this point, not expecting any \naccumulation.&&",
